reference-goldens.jsonl
=======================

288 serving-level golden cases for the `beam` template, extracted unchanged (fields reduced to
id / source / prefix / chunks / tools / serving / serving_batch) from the model builder's frozen
differential corpus `lib/response-template/tests/data/{generated,tags}.jsonl` on their Dynamo
reference branch (commit cb95d1dfd5e05f2217f1ca9c956fbca766006f22). Only cases whose
`template` is absent or byte-identical to the built-in Beam `response_template` were kept.

The expectations were recorded from the builder's Python reference implementation, not from any
Dynamo parser. They are an ORACLE for argument typing and split-invariance; where this crate's
parser goals intentionally differ (for example, never leaking tool markup into content), the
divergence is listed with a reason in `reference-known-divergences.yaml`.

